   "updated_at": "2026-11-11T18:01:05Z",
   "body": "One more residual, from the round-3 review of #812, to weigh with this issue:\n\n`check` accepts a forged message cell after a mood when the member closes the row and the table and then opens a plain `<table>`:\n\n`Mood removed.</span></td><td class=\"messCase2\">…</td></tr></table><table><tr><td>`\n\n`check` passes it; the redactor raises on the raw form. The README residual says \"then a message table\", which is narrower than this. Two ways to close it: have `check` refuse any `td.messCase2` after a mood that is not followed by HFR's own closing of its message, or widen the README wording.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
